## Troubleshooting

### GPU Not Detected

```bash
# Check ROCm installation
rocm-smi

# Check PyTorch sees GPU
python -c "import torch; print(torch.cuda.is_available())"

# If False, reinstall PyTorch with ROCm
pip install torch --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/rocm6.2
```

### Slow Inference (>10s per essay)

```bash
# Set environment variables
export HSA_OVERRIDE_GFX_VERSION=11.0.0
export PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True

# Restart Python and try again
```

### Out of Memory

```bash
# Your 24GB VRAM is plenty!
# But if it happens, reduce batch size or use 4-bit quantization
# (already enabled in 05_test_llama.py)
```

### Dataset Not Found

```bash
# Check path in config.py
nano config.py
# Update DATASET_ROOT to match your location

# Or create symlink
ln -s /path/to/dataset ~/datasets/write-and-improve-corpus-2024-v2
```

